1
00:00:00,349 --> 00:00:03,719
(Amy:)The kind who almost put a pillow
over your face last night.

2
00:00:05,354 --> 00:00:06,654
(Sheldon:)Wow.

3
00:00:06,722 --> 00:00:08,622
(Sheldon:)I anticipated
we'd have problems,

4
00:00:08,691 --> 00:00:12,231
(Sheldon:)but I never thought your
scientific rigor would be one of them.

5
00:00:12,295 --> 00:00:15,795
(Amy:)I'm sorry, are you questioning
my integrity as a scientist?

6
00:00:15,865 --> 00:00:18,835
(Sheldon:)If the lab room
disposable shoe cover fits.

7
00:00:20,002 --> 00:00:21,672
(Penny:)Was that a science diss?

8
00:00:21,737 --> 00:00:22,907
(Bernadette:)- Yeah.
- Was it a good one?

9
00:00:22,972 --> 00:00:24,672
- Eh.
- Ah.

10
00:00:24,740 --> 00:00:26,270
(Amy:)What would a
theoretical physicist

11
00:00:26,342 --> 00:00:28,142
(Amy:)understand about an
experiment anyway?

12
00:00:28,211 --> 00:00:30,091
(Amy:)I mean, you wouldn't know
a confounding variable

13
00:00:30,146 --> 00:00:33,286
(Amy:)if two of them hit you in
the face at the same time!

14
00:00:34,851 --> 00:00:36,381
(Amy:)And you don't even
get that joke,

15
00:00:36,452 --> 00:00:39,692
(Amy:)'cause you don't even work
with confounding variables!

16
00:00:40,556 --> 00:00:42,186
(Sheldon:)How dare you?

17
00:00:42,258 --> 00:00:44,388
(Amy:)Oh, you heard me.
Your experimental bona fides

18
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:45,690
(Amy:)are laughable.

19
00:00:45,761 --> 00:00:48,431
(Sheldon:)Whoa, whoa! Now you're
making fun of my bona fides?

20
00:00:48,498 --> 00:00:51,238
(Amy:)Can't make fun of something
that's a null set.

21
00:00:52,368 --> 00:00:53,868
(Leonard:)I feel like

22
00:00:53,936 --> 00:00:55,336
I should say "damn."
- Do it.

23
00:00:55,404 --> 00:00:57,034
Damn!

24
00:00:57,106 --> 00:01:00,336
(Sheldon:)Well, if you are so protective
of the scientific method,

25
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:02,070
(Sheldon:)perhaps we should use
the next five weeks

26
00:01:02,090 --> 00:01:03,910
(Sheldon:)to finish what we started.

27
00:01:03,913 --> 00:01:05,913
Well, for science, maybe I will!

28
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:07,482
For science, maybe you should!

29
00:01:07,550 --> 00:01:08,250
- Fine!
- Fine!

30
00:01:08,317 --> 00:01:09,847
(Leonard:)- Good.
- Great.

31
00:01:09,919 --> 00:01:11,989
(Amy:)Do you want to go to our place
and make out?

32
00:01:12,054 --> 00:01:13,854
(Sheldon:)Does Stephen Hawking roll
through the quad?

33
00:01:20,963 --> 00:01:53,003
The new neighbors
are weird.

